bip32 — third-party attribution
====================================================================

This file carries a CONDITION, added 2026-09-09. `src/bip32_vectors.zig` and
`src/bip39_vectors.zig` reproduce third-party test vectors under two different
licences. Redistributing this module — alone, or as part of zig-libs — must
keep this file with it.

⛔ THIS FILE WAS ALREADY BEING POINTED AT. Both vector files carry the line
"see NOTICE / SPEC.md for provenance" in their own headers, and
`modules/bip32/NOTICE` did not exist — a pointer to nothing, in the one file a
reader consults to answer "what do I owe?". `README.md`'s `Provenance:`
statement made it worse by answering a narrower question and sounding like the
whole one: "no `NOTICE` entry required for the BIP-39/BIP-32 algorithms
themselves". True of the algorithms, silent about the vectors.

The gate written for exactly this shape could not see the vectors:
`check-catalog`'s data-file claim looked for a committed file that is neither
Zig source nor documentation, and these went through transcription into `.zig`,
so no witness was found and the check never ran. That hole was closed on
2026-09-09; this file is one of the four records it forced.

No code changed, and none needs to. The vectors are unaltered, and the
condition has been in force since they were committed.

